  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Perched on the hills above Saint-Tropez with an open view over the gulf, this luxury château-hotel (Airelles collection) has extensive grounds, a spa and an outdoor pool — and welcomes dogs for a high-end stay in Saint-Tropez. Stays include a gourmet breakfast, an in-room minibar, access to the Airelles by Valmont spa, mattresses and parasols on the private Jardin Tropézina beach (by reservation) and transfers to the beach or the town centre, according to the suite pages on airelles.com. The Grimaud-Provence tourist office lists 63 suites.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>The official site states on each suite page: “At La Messardière, our four-legged friends are also our guests, at no extra charge”. The welcome includes a cosy bed, treats, a personalised menu, pet-sitting services and surprise gifts. The site publishes no size or breed limit and does not say whether dogs may enter the pool, spa, private beach or restaurants: ask when booking on 04 94 56 76 00. Pampelonne beach, Tahiti area, is about 2.2 km away, under 10 minutes by car.</p>
      <p>The hotel is seasonal: open from 30 April to 11 October 2026 according to Grimaud Provence Tourisme. Check the dates of your season before booking.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the dog's welcome is free and quite pampered (bed, treats, dedicated menu) per the official site — just ask about pool, private beach and restaurant access when booking.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Saint-Tropez's historic centre, with its lanes and yacht harbour, is easy to visit by car or shuttle from the hills above — the <a href="/en/fiche-plages-centre-ville-saint-tropez">town-centre beaches</a> and the <a href="/en/fiche-activite-marche-place-des-lices-saint-tropez">Place des Lices market</a> are not to be missed. By the sea, <a href="/en/fiche-pampelonne">Pampelonne beach</a> and the beach restaurant <a href="/en/fiche-restaurant-le-migon">Le Migon</a> round out the outing nicely.</p>
